{# Route registry lives in src/_data/routes.js. `routes.nav` is the pre-filtered subset that belongs
in the nav: home is absent because it is reachable via the site title link, exactly as it is today,
and Nunjucks cannot call .filter() so the subset is computed in the data file rather than here.
Paths come from the registry, so the flip from /gallery.html to /gallery/ landed in one place. NOTE:
keep angle brackets out of these Nunjucks comments. Prettier's HTML printer parses tag names inside
them as real markup and mangles the file. The list items are wrapped in a ul: they were direct
children of nav, which is invalid HTML and costs assistive technology the list semantics (a screen
reader could not say how many items the navigation has). role="list" is not redundant here - Safari
drops the implicit list role from any list carrying list-style: none, which header nav ul does. The
current page is marked aria-current="page". The whole anchor is duplicated across the branches
rather than conditionally emitting a single attribute: prettier parses this file with its HTML
parser, which mangles a Nunjucks tag that sits inside an element's attribute list. #}
<nav id="site-nav" aria-label="Main">
    <ul role="list">
        {%- for p in routes.nav %}{% if p.key == key %}
        <li><a href="{{ p.path }}" aria-current="page">{{ p.label }}</a></li>
        {%- else %}
        <li><a href="{{ p.path }}">{{ p.label }}</a></li>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
</nav>
